BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Other Choice
DTSTART:20260225T003000Z
DTEND:20260225T030500Z
DTSTAMP:20260225T003000Z
UID:kPwECEsm9m
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 139 mins (2h19m)\n\nIn his diabolical new thriller\,
  Park Chan-wook crafts a dark fable about the cutthroat nature of contempo
 rary work culture\, starring Lee Byung Hun as a husband and father who tak
 es violent action after being laid off. Nominated for three Golden Globes
  including Best Motion Picture - Musical or Comedy.\n\nhttps://www.siff.ne
 t/cinema/in-theaters/no-other-choice\n\nEstimated start: 16:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Moment
DTSTART:20260225T034500Z
DTEND:20260225T055500Z
DTSTAMP:20260225T034500Z
UID:IhYZjlvtHb
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nA rising pop star navigates the 
 complexities of fame and industry pressure while preparing for her arena t
 our debut.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/the-moment\n\nEstima
 ted start: 20:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Oscar Shorts: Animated
DTSTART:20260226T001000Z
DTEND:20260226T023500Z
DTSTAMP:20260226T001000Z
UID:Y0xwDJC7qh
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 130 mins (2h10m)\n\nFor the 21st consecutive year\, 
 ShortsTV presents the Oscar-Nominated Short Films\, opening on February 20
 . With all three categories offered – Animated\, Live Action\, and Docum
 entary – this is your annual chance to predict the winners (and have the
  edge in your Oscar pool)! A perennial hit with audiences around the count
 ry and the world\, don’t miss this year’s selection of shorts. The Aca
 demy Awards take place Sunday\, March 15.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/i
 n-theaters/2026-oscar-nominated-shorts/2026-oscar-nominated-shorts-animati
 on\n\nEstimated start: 16:25
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Magellan
DTSTART:20260226T024500Z
DTEND:20260226T055500Z
DTSTAMP:20260226T024500Z
UID:D1iMV4wn1u
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 173 mins (2h53m)\n\nEvery astonishing visual composi
 tion carries historical and political weight in the monumental new film fr
 om singular Filipino filmmaker Lav Diaz\, who mounts an absorbing story of
  colonial conquest and obsession\, starring Gael García Bernal as Ferdina
 nd Magellan.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/magellan\n\nEstima
 ted start: 19:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
